The `(int)` cast on `get_option( CLEARANCE_PAGE_OPTION )` in `clearance_section_label_hook` existed to handle numeric strings returned by caching layers, but it is unnecessary given a proper type guard.

## Changes

- **`includes/admin-page-list-table.php` — `clearance_section_label_hook`**: Drop the `(int)` cast. An `is_int()` guard returns early for any non-integer option value (e.g. `false` when the option is absent), ensuring the direct `$post->ID === $page_id` strict comparison remains type-safe without a cast:

```php
// Before
$page_id = (int) get_option( CLEARANCE_PAGE_OPTION );
if ( $page_id > 0 && $post->ID === $page_id ) { ... }

// After
$page_id = get_option( CLEARANCE_PAGE_OPTION );
if ( ! is_int( $page_id ) ) {
    return $post_states;
}
if ( $page_id > 0 && $post->ID === $page_id ) { ... }
```

The cast inside `clearance_page_exists` is intentionally preserved. The `(int)` cast in `run_create_clearance_page_tool` is also preserved, as that function is being refactored separately in PR #119.

